## Original Content
Plus, what Justice Thomas said on Sen. Ted Cruz’s podcast.

## Summary
The Supreme Court (SCOTUS) sided with the Trump administration in a legal dispute involving mail-in voting. Additionally, Justice Clarence Thomas commented on the issue during an appearance on Senator Ted Cruz's podcast.

## Key Points
- The Supreme Court ruled in favor of the Trump administration regarding a mail-in voting challenge.
- This decision pertains to legal and procedural aspects of mail-in voting in elections.
- Justice Thomas discussed related topics on a political podcast hosted by Senator Ted Cruz.
- The outcome may influence future policies on voting methods and election integrity.


